Limbo Emulator (QEMU) for Android -- QEMU 11 port

================================================================================

1. What is this?

A fork of limboemu/limbo (app v6.0.1, commit 887c6a6) with the bundled QEMU
upgraded from 5.1.0 to 11.0.3. See ../docs/limbo-x86-qemu11-port-plan.md for
the full analysis and UPSTREAM.md for provenance.

Two things changed fundamentally compared to upstream Limbo:

  * 64-bit only. QEMU 11.0 removed every 32-bit host backend, so armeabi-v7a
    and x86 cannot be built at all. Use upstream Limbo 6.0.1 for those.

  * The native build is meson/ninja, not make. QEMU deleted Makefile.target in
    5.2, which is where upstream Limbo injected its shared-library link rule.

===============================================================================

2. Requirements

    Android SDK, build-tools 35
    Android NDK r27c or newer (clang only; the gcc path is gone)
    JDK 17 (required by AGP 8)
    Linux host (Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 tested)

    meson >= 1.5, ninja, python >= 3.9, pkg-config, curl, patch

    sudo apt-get install meson ninja-build python3 pkg-config curl patch

===============================================================================

3. Configuration

    limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni/android-config/android-limbo-config.mak

    At minimum set NDK_ROOT. BUILD_HOST must be arm64-v8a or x86_64.

===============================================================================

4. Get and patch QEMU

    cd limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni
    curl -fSLO https://download.qemu.org/qemu-11.0.3.tar.xz
    tar -xJf qemu-11.0.3.tar.xz
    mv qemu-11.0.3 qemu
    cd qemu && patch -p1 < ../patches/qemu-11.0.3.patch

    Unlike upstream Limbo you do NOT need to download glib, libffi, pixman or
    SDL2 by hand: android-config/build-deps.sh cross-compiles glib (with
    libffi, pcre2 and proxy-libintl as meson subprojects), pixman and libslirp,
    and points pkg-config at the NDK's own libz.

===============================================================================

5. Build

    cd limbo-android-lib/src/main/jni
    export BUILD_HOST=arm64-v8a
    export BUILD_GUEST=x86_64-softmmu
    make limbo

    Useful individual targets:

        make check-tools    verify meson/ninja/pkg-config/NDK are usable
        make deps           cross-build glib, pixman, libslirp
        make config-qemu    run QEMU's configure (generates the meson build dir)
        make qemu           ninja the emulator library + copy pc-bios assets
        make install        stage into limbo-android-x86/src/main/jniLibs
        make distclean      remove the build dirs and the dependency prefix

    Output:

        limbo-android-lib/src/main/jniLibs/<ABI>/
            libcompat-limbo.so, libSDL2.so, liblimbo.so, ...

        limbo-android-x86/src/main/jniLibs/<ABI>/
            libqemu-system-x86_64.so

    IMPORTANT: every NEEDED entry of libqemu-system-*.so must be an
    unversioned platform library (libc.so, libm.so, libdl.so, liblog.so).
    Android's package installer does not extract lib*.so.N from an APK, so a
    dependency with a versioned soname builds fine and then fails to load on
    device. "make install" prints the NEEDED list so you can check. This is
    why glib/pixman/libslirp are linked statically.

===============================================================================

6. Build the APK

    export ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=~/Android/Sdk
    ./gradlew assembleRelease

===============================================================================

7. How the emulator is loaded

    Android forbids exec'ing binaries from an app's private directory (W^X,
    enforced from API 29), so QEMU is built as a shared library and loaded
    with dlopen(). The meson patch turns

        executable('qemu-system-x86_64', ...)

    into

        shared_library('qemu-system-x86_64', ...)

    behind the new -Dshared_emulator option, and jni/limbo/vm-executor-jni.c
    resolves and calls:

        void qemu_init(int argc, char **argv);
        int  qemu_main_loop(void);
        void qemu_cleanup(int status);

    These signatures changed after QEMU 5.1 -- keep vm-executor-jni.c in sync
    when upgrading QEMU. The same applies to the ShutdownCause values in
    vm-executor-jni.h, which mirror qapi/run-state.json.

    Disk images opened through the Storage Access Framework are routed through
    Limbo's helpers with linker --wrap (see android-qemu-config.mak). Upstream
    Limbo did this by rewriting static archives with objcopy --redefine-sym
    from inside Makefile.target; there is no such hook in a meson build.

===============================================================================

8. Development notes

    a. Android-compatibility changes in QEMU are tagged __LIMBO__.

    b. Configuration files:
        android-config/android-limbo-config.mak       user-facing settings
        android-config/android-qemu-config.mak        configure command line
        android-config/android-qemu-config-11.0.3.mak QEMU 11 feature flags
        android-config/gen-meson-cross.sh             meson cross file generator
        android-config/build-deps.sh                  dependency cross-build

    c. Makefiles:
        Makefile, Android.mk, Application.mk, android-limbo-build.mak

       android-qemu-build.mak is gone: it existed only to be included from
       QEMU's Makefile.target.

    d. Frontend UI options: Config.java

===============================================================================

9. Known gaps in this port

    * SDL frontend is not enabled yet: patches/sdl2-2.0.8.patch still targets
      SDL2 2.0.8 and has to be forward-ported (2.32.x is current). Until then
      build with USE_SDL=false and use the VNC frontend.

    * Only x86_64-softmmu is wired up. Other guests need libfdt cross-built
      into the dependency prefix.

    * KVM is compiled in but effectively unused: almost no retail Android
      device exposes /dev/kvm. QEMU falls back to TCG at run time.

===============================================================================

